loper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bdb35a4a91916c18bd3d9d00fa5be36c237dafd79d5fe92bc622d7d61b6eb23" "basis" 1131 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bdb35a4a91916c18bd3d9d00fa5be36c237dafd79d5fe92bc622d7d61b6eb23" "basis" 1131 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-9980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $\\frac{2}{5}.$ Find the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-9980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(k-2)-3(4-6)+1(4-3k) \\\\  & =2k-4+6+4-3k \\\\  & =6-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(4-6) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6-k}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6-k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{21}^{′}=\\frac{2}{5}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{6-k} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 2\\cdot 5 & =2(6-k) \\\\ 10 & =12-2k \\\\ 2k & =2 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-9980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29f08a094a004abb8d877401a296bd4159983078a2d99bdcc488d890156c1a25"} {"question" "q-9980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-9980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-9980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-18287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ if its determinant is $24.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-18287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =24-0 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31}=\\frac{1}{24}\\cdot 24=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-18287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29f08a094a004abb8d877401a296bd4159983078a2d99bdcc488d890156c1a25"} {"question" "q-18287" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-18287" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{12}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{24}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{12}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-18287" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-103533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-103533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-103533" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29f08a094a004abb8d877401a296bd4159983078a2d99bdcc488d890156c1a25"} {"question" "q-103533" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-103533" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-103533" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-319437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $det(A)=k-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-319437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=k-1\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-1+2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-1}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{k-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{k-1} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ k-1 & =-2 \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-319437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29f08a094a004abb8d877401a296bd4159983078a2d99bdcc488d890156c1a25"} {"question" "q-319437" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-319437" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-319546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nif its determinant is $17.$\n\n${a}_{13}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-319546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\,1\\cdot (1\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-319546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29f08a094a004abb8d877401a296bd4159983078a2d99bdcc488d890156c1a25"} {"question" "q-319546" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064809/state.json" "file_sha256" "92dfcfd71a9b6fe4d179997ce06d49f5c2bad8102be9694caf2e1c329bb4dabe"} {"question" "q-319546" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{17}"] "cat